{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Phase 9Y schema-security classification for every table in schema 'public'. Captured from the EFFECTIVE database catalog, not parsed from migration text \u2014 because the exposure this file exists to prevent (workflow_stories) was created by a migration that simply never mentioned row level security, so migration text alone could never have revealed it.",
    "captured_from": "production project iboepohjwrhtgshrqaol",
    "captured_at": "2026-09-10",
    "total_tables": 70,
    "workflow_stories_note": "Its row reflects the state established by supabase/migrations/20260909120000_workflow_stories_rls.sql. Every other row is as-observed.",
    "regenerate": "Introspect pg_class.relrowsecurity, pg_policies and information_schema.role_table_grants for schema 'public' and rewrite this file. lib/qa/schema-security-invariant.test.ts defines the exact contract each entry must satisfy.",
    "classes": {
      "SERVER_ONLY": "Service-role only. anon and authenticated hold NO grants at all. RLS must be enabled.",
      "TENANT_RLS": "Reached by user-bound clients under an owner-rooted policy. Default Supabase grants remain and are inert because RLS gates every row. RLS must be enabled and at least one policy must exist.",
      "INTERNAL_DENY_ALL": "RLS enabled with zero policies: default-deny for anon and authenticated. Grants remain but reach nothing. Safe; revoking them too would be belt-and-braces.",
      "INTENTIONALLY_PUBLIC": "Deliberately reachable without a session. Requires an explicit reviewed entry and may hold SELECT only, never DML. NONE exist today \u2014 the class is declared so a future one is a deliberate, reviewed act rather than a silent default."
    },
    "limitations": [
      "This is a point-in-time capture. A change made directly in the Supabase dashboard after capture is not detected until the file is regenerated.",
      "It records grants and RLS state, not policy semantics: a policy that is present but wrongly written is out of scope here and is covered by the route-level isolation suites.",
      "The paired migration-text rule in the invariant is forward-looking only; it governs tables created from now on.",
      "The registry is a live-catalog snapshot, so a migration-created table that is not live is absent by construction; _meta.created_not_live records those and the invariant requires each to declare RLS."
    ],
    "out_of_band_rls": {
      "tables": [],
      "meaning": "Empty since Phase 9Z. It previously held dream_issues, whose RLS existed in production but was declared in no migration. Closure audit #4 showed that was not an isolated case and not merely documentation debt: a database rebuilt from repo SQL created dream_issues, cost_rates and morning_briefings with RLS OFF and anon DML live. supabase/migrations/20260910090000_declarative_rls_parity.sql declares all three, so the exception has no remaining subject.",
      "rule": "An entry here excuses a table from the migration-text rule. It must still be RLS-enabled in effective state, and it should be treated as temporary: an exception that outlives its cause is a hole with a comment next to it."
    },
    "created_not_live": {
      "tables": [
        "agent_decisions",
        "ai_cost_snapshots",
        "memory_refs"
      ],
      "meaning": "Created by a migration but absent from the production catalog at capture time \u2014 never applied there, or dropped out-of-band. They are NOT a fresh-deploy hazard: each declares RLS in its own migration, so a rebuild creates them protected. Listed so their absence from the table map is a recorded fact rather than a silent gap, and so the fail-closed rule can distinguish them from a genuinely new unprotected table.",
      "requirement": "Every entry must have RLS declared in the migration corpus.",
      "classes": {
        "agent_decisions": "SERVER_ONLY",
        "ai_cost_snapshots": "SERVER_ONLY",
        "memory_refs": "SERVER_ONLY"
      },
      "classes_note": "Phase 9AA. The migration security gate needs a class for every table a migration touches. These three are not live, so they cannot be introspected; Phase 9AB made all three server-only (policies dropped, client grants revoked) and no application code reads them, so SERVER_ONLY is their intended class."
    },
    "post_migration": "20260909120000_workflow_stories_rls.sql (Phase 9Y) and 20260910090000_declarative_rls_parity.sql (Phase 9Z). Every row reflects effective production state, which those two migrations now also declare; and 20260910120000_cost_ledger_rls_isolation.sql (Phase 9AB), which moves cost_events and infra_costs from TENANT_RLS to SERVER_ONLY: their `project_id IS NULL OR \u2026` policies on role public are dropped and anon/authenticated grants revoked.",
    "views": "Phase 9AA. Public VIEWS, classified like tables. A view runs as its owner unless it is security_invoker, so base-table RLS does not protect it; the migration security gate fails any client-reachable public view without security_invoker and any public view absent from this map. `live` records whether it exists in production."
  },
